{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Mandate wheelchair-accessible emergency safety zones in motorway barriers",
        "additional_details": "Current motorway guidance (\u201cGo Left, Get Safe\u201d) instructs drivers to exit their vehicles and wait behind the barrier, but standard steel and concrete barriers are impossible for paraplegic and wheelchair\u2011using drivers to cross. On motorways without a hard shoulder, this leaves disabled motorists trapped in live lanes or narrow refuge areas. Installing accessible rear\u2011opening gates or roll\u2011through alcoves at intervals would provide a safe, equal escape route for all.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to require National Highways to install wheelchair\u2011accessible emergency gates, ramps or lowered alcoves along motorway barriers, especially where no hard shoulder exists. The Department for Transport should update the DMRB to ensure disabled drivers can also reach safety.",
